model {
  extend basalt.modelGateway {
    metadata {
      constraint "Pool availability monitoring is absent from deployment until an explicit target is configured. A one-minute cron reads that pool's uncached account view, durable acknowledgement and exact native revision without warming, renewing, reconciling, installing or dispatching inference. Failed renewal remains visible even while acknowledged policy serves through grace. Runtime and view failures cannot suppress the separate guard observation. Each run has a bounded deadline and sends paired check-ins, with fixed guard and reason diagnostics on failure. A failure's error event is sent once per episode, compared by guard and reason only: an availability episode starts when a run's set of failures differs from the one last reported and ends with the first run whose set differs again, a passing run included; a reliability reason's episode starts when it starts failing and ends with the first run without it. The pool records what it reported in its own storage after sending, so a start whose events were refused is sent again, and a run that cannot read that record within its bound reports on the quarter hour only. The opening check-in of every run defines the cron monitor in the observability adapter: the Worker's own every-minute cron in UTC, a one-minute margin and runtime, an incident after three failed check-ins in a row and recovery after one success. While a target is configured, each run restores that definition and a hand edit lasts until the next check-in. Cron incident envelopes carry the Worker release and a bounded runtime observation from the same passive probe, including observed boot, running state and selected application version when known. An expected selected boot stays separate from an observed boot. Legacy runtime APIs expose no application version, and Worker image configuration is not proof of the running image, so unavailable identities remain explicit. Sampling adds no runtime or provider reads and never suppresses an outage. Privacy verification rejects private diagnostic values and invalid status sentinels in every envelope field, while accepting measured durations containing the same digits. Who is notified, and how, stays in the adapter's alert rules. Production activation requires a separately approved exact target plan."
    }
  }
  extend basalt.poolRuntime {
    metadata {
      constraint "The management-authenticated native policy check runs the scheduler admission predicate against its current immutable registry and a fresh signed revision assertion with no candidates. It does not install policy, extend a deadline, select an account, refresh the plugin health lease or issue inference. The separate runtime health lease remains required. Unknown, dirty, expired and different revisions refuse this check."
    }
  }
}
